<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="yes"?>
<!--
  The id stays `script.embuary.info` on purpose, and it is load-bearing three
  times over:

    * `context.embuary.info` declares `<import addon="script.embuary.info"/>`,
      a hard dependency Kodi enforces at install time;
    * skin.contuary references the id ~28 times across its XML;
    * it is what lets Kodi upgrade an existing install in place, for users who
      have set "Update official add-ons from" to "Any repositories".

  That last one is the whole distribution story. `script.embuary.info` 2.0.8 is
  in repository.xbmc.org, so Kodi's AddonRepos::DoAddonUpdateCheck checks
  official repos first, finds nothing above 2.0.8, and only then falls through
  to private repos — and only when addons.updatemode == ANY_REPOSITORY. Users on
  the default setting keep upstream 2.0.8 and never see this build.

  Version 2.1.0 clears both upstream's released 2.0.8 and the unreleased 2.0.10
  on its matrix branch, which is what this fork is based on. If upstream ever
  revives above 2.1.0 the official repo reclaims the add-on, which is the right
  failsafe rather than a problem to engineer around.

  The display name is plain "Embuary Info". It carried a "(Kontell)" suffix so
  nobody would file our bugs against sualfred, but that job is done by the
  summary and description below, which name the fork and where to report to;
  the suffix only made the name awkward everywhere it is shown. provider-name
  still says kontell, and Kodi shows that on the add-on's information page.
-->
<addon id="script.embuary.info" name="Embuary Info" version="2.4.0" provider-name="kontell">
    <!--
      script.module.requests is gone: nothing imports it any more. Its 825 ms
      import was the largest single cost in opening a page, and what it was
      being used for is four plain GETs and a HEAD; see
      resources/lib/http_session.py.

      arrow stays, but only widgets.py needs it now, for a locale-aware long
      date on the plugin path. The info dialog no longer imports it.
    -->
    <requires>
        <import addon="xbmc.python" version="3.0.0"/>
        <import addon="script.module.arrow" version="0.10.0"/>
        <import addon="script.module.simplecache" version="2.0.2" />
        <import addon="script.module.routing" version="0.2.0"/>
    </requires>
    <extension point="xbmc.python.pluginsource" library="plugin.py">
      <provides>video</provides>
    </extension>
    <extension point="xbmc.python.script" library="default.py">
        <provides>executable</provides>
    </extension>
    <extension point="xbmc.service" library="service.py" />
    <extension point="xbmc.addon.metadata">
        <!--
          Reuse the Python interpreter between invocations instead of tearing
          it down each time.

          It is parsed only here. Under xbmc.python.pluginsource, where it
          reads as though it belongs, AddonInfoBuilder never looks at it and
          nothing is logged either way.

          What it buys, measured on this Kodi 21.3: opening a movie page warm
          takes 1642 ms, of which 1175 ms is imports and 825 ms of that is
          `import requests` alone. A parked interpreter keeps sys.modules, so
          the second and later launches skip all of it.

          Reuse is opportunistic, not guaranteed: Kodi keeps one reusable
          invoker thread system-wide and gives it up as soon as any other
          script runs. So the cold path still has to be worth something on its
          own, and the import cost above is still worth attacking.

          Three things had to be true before this could be turned on, all of
          them silent failures otherwise:

            * plugin.py refreshes plugin.handle from sys.argv, because
              script.module.routing captures it at import and run() does not
              re-read it.
            * The action routes close their handle. Kodi's wait loop for a
              script has no timeout, and a parked invoker never reports the
              script as finished, so a missing endOfDirectory becomes an
              unbounded hang rather than a harmless omission.
            * Settings are read per launch rather than into module constants,
              or a parked module keeps the first launch's values forever.

          One consequence for development: copying new files in does not take
          effect while an interpreter is parked with the old modules in
          sys.modules. Disable and re-enable the add-on to discard it.
        -->
        <reuselanguageinvoker>true</reuselanguageinvoker>
        <platform>all</platform>
        <license>Apache-2.0</license>
        <source>https://github.com/kontell/script.embuary.info</source>
        <assets>
            <icon>resources/icon.png</icon>
            <fanart>resources/fanart.jpg</fanart>
        </assets>
        <news>v2.4.0
- Settings are three tabs, General, Filters and Skin, with no headings inside
  them. Filters is new and holds everything that drops an item from a list.
  Existing settings keep their values.
- The rating and votes filters start switched on, at 4.0 and 5. Both shipped at
  zero, which keeps everything, so neither did anything until you found them.
  New installs only: Kodi keeps a stored value over a changed default.
- The votes slider is 0-500 in fives, down from 0-5000 in hundreds.
- Opening an actor no longer asks which person you meant when the answer is
  obvious, and a name resolved once is remembered. A new button in General
  forgets them again if one was matched to the wrong person.
- "Allow items of the next [n] days" sits directly below "Hide upcoming items"
  and disappears with it rather than greying out.
- The rating badge on posters sits further in from the corner.
</news>
        <summary lang="en_GB">Embuary Info Script (Kontell fork)</summary>
        <summary lang="de_DE">Embuary Info Script (Kontell-Fork)</summary>
        <description lang="en_GB">Helper script to provide The Movie DB informations for persons, shows and movies. Works best with a skin integration.

Kontell fork of sualfred's Embuary Info, maintained at https://github.com/kontell/script.embuary.info — please report issues there rather than to the original author. Fixes unbounded memory growth when browsing many pages in one session, and reduces artwork bandwidth and page-load time.</description>
        <description lang="de_DE">Helfer Script das Abfragen von The Movie DB informationen für Personen, Serien und Filme zu ermöglichen. Funktioniert am besten mit einer Skin Integration.

Kontell-Fork von sualfreds Embuary Info, gepflegt unter https://github.com/kontell/script.embuary.info — Fehler bitte dort melden, nicht beim ursprünglichen Autor.</description>
    </extension>
</addon>
